{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1097178-confucius-is-a-god","id":1097178,"title":"Confucius Is A God?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-26T10:47:19-07:00","id":1097178,"title":"Confucius Is A God?","content":"In the latest Kickstarter Preview we discover that Confucius has become a god, and actively sends his Scions around to convince people he is not. This seems like a pretty hot topic. Discuss!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T11:19:38-07:00","id":1097191,"title":"","content":"On a related note:<br /> <br /> Is it just me, or is the Shen's write-up the goofiest yet?<br /> <br /> Random Immortal: ...My liege.<br /> <br /> Huangdi: *twitching* Yes?<br /> <br /> RI: Did an airliner just shave off the top of your pagoda?<br /> <br /> H: For the fifth time this year? Yes.<br /> <br /> RI: And you had just moved your collection of restored Ming vases there?<br /> <br /> H: That is accurate.<br /> <br /> RI: ...my liege, I don't believe it would be improper to swear in this one instance.<br /> <br /> H: You have my gratitude. Ahem: <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>FUUUUUUU-</b></span><br /> <br /> (elsewhere)<br /> <br /> Nuwa: *gazes stoically at the magnitude 6 earthquake* It appears my vacation just ended...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T11:25:35-07:00","id":1097194,"title":"","content":"The distinction between a god and a ghost can be rather blurred in Chinese folk religion, so sure, why not?<br /> <br /> There are some choices that bother me because of personal preferences. For example, I prefer the version of the story in which Houyi became tyrannical after losing his wife, though the seeds were always there in his impetuous personality. Furthermore, I think it's odd that Erlang's write-up doesn't mention the story that his mother was imprisoned beneath a mountain for breaking the rules against god-mortal interaction, which adds new dimensions to his somewhat standoffish relationship with divine officialdom.<br /> <br /> However, there are also some choices that just seem strange to me. For example, the Queen Mother of the West is indeed one of the oldest members of the Chinese pantheon, but I have a hard time seeing her as a Primordial when she interacted so much with both gods and mortals on a regular basis. She's a regular participant in the feasts of heaven. Furthermore she's taken mortal lovers as recently as Emperor Wu of Han, who was well into historical times at around the same period as Marius and Sulla over in Rome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1607-creticus","name":"Creticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T11:40:33-07:00","id":1097198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Creticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1097178-confucius-is-a-god?p=1097194#post1097194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The distinction between a god and a ghost can be rather blurred in Chinese folk religion, so sure, why not?<br /> <br /> There are some choices that bother me because of personal preferences. For example, I prefer the version of the story in which Houyi became tyrannical after losing his wife, though the seeds were always there in his impetuous personality. Furthermore, I think it's odd that Erlang's write-up doesn't mention the story that his mother was imprisoned beneath a mountain for breaking the rules against god-mortal interaction, which adds new dimensions to his somewhat standoffish relationship with divine officialdom.<br /> <br /> However, there are also some choices that just seem strange to me. For example, the <b>Queen Mother of the West</b> is indeed one of the oldest members of the Chinese pantheon, but I have a hard time seeing her as a Primordial when she interacted so much with both gods and mortals on a regular basis. She's a regular participant in the feasts of heaven. Furthermore she's taken mortal lovers as recently as Emperor Wu of Han, who was well into historical times at around the same period as Marius and Sulla over in Rome.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, they note she has a human form that many people don't realize is just a mask for the whirling storm she is. So presumably she's in that form when talking with people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T11:56:50-07:00","id":1097203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1097178-confucius-is-a-god?p=1097198#post1097198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, they note she has a human form that many people don't realize is just a mask for the whirling storm she is. So presumably she's in that form when talking with people.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was under the impression that Primordials are distant, powerful figures who don't interact much with the rest of their pantheon. For example, Nyx, who was strong enough to make Zeus cautious but has no speaking role in Greek mythology, or Danu, who was ancestor to the Tuatha de Danann but doesn't actually show up in what stories remain to us.<br /> <br /> In contrast, the Queen Mother of the West is very, very active. She's the one who gives Houyi the elixir of immortality in exchange for his architectural skills; she parties with the other senior members of the pantheon while eating food grown in her gardens; and she likes having affairs with some of the most famous rulers in Chinese history, who receive the chance to become immortal but invariably fail to heed her advice because of their mortal preoccupations.<br /> <br /> What does her form matter?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1607-creticus","name":"Creticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T12:04:01-07:00","id":1097206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Creticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1097178-confucius-is-a-god?p=1097203#post1097203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was under the impression that Primordials are distant, powerful figures who don't interact much with the rest of their pantheon. For example, Nyx, who was strong enough to make Zeus cautious but has no speaking role in Greek mythology, or Danu, who was ancestor to the Tuatha de Danann but doesn't actually show up in what stories remain to us.<br /> <br /> In contrast, the Queen Mother of the West is very, very active. She's the one who gives Houyi the elixir of immortality in exchange for his architectural skills; she parties with the other senior members of the pantheon while eating food grown in her gardens; and she likes having affairs with some of the most famous rulers in Chinese history, who receive the chance to become immortal but invariably fail to heed her advice because of their mortal preoccupations.<br /> <br /> What does her form matter?</div> </div> </div> </div>Setting aside the fact that exact details may still change, we already know that not all Primordials follow the Primordial rules... Primordials apparently never have Scions, but Kitchi-Manitou and Danu both do... so the Queen Mother might simply be a Primordial who breaks the 'never interacts with Humanity' rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T12:26:49-07:00","id":1097217,"title":"","content":"Stuff like Confucius and Xi Wangmu I might have imagined differently myself, but both are presented in a way where I can more than easily accept that. All together, I think this is the most well-crafted Pantheon yet, it really gives off the feel you get from reading traditional Chinese literature. I hope it shows the direction all of the Pantheons will be developing into as they go through the revision process. I really had fun reading this, both for the loving detail of the info and the style.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T12:49:59-07:00","id":1097233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1097178-confucius-is-a-god?p=1097206#post1097206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Setting aside the fact that exact details may still change, we already know that not all Primordials follow the Primordial rules... Primordials apparently never have Scions, but Kitchi-Manitou and Danu both do... so the Queen Mother might simply be a Primordial who breaks the 'never interacts with Humanity' rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds messy, though to be fair, mythology isn't easily categorized.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, I actually remember Erlang getting along pretty well with Sun Wukong after he became Xuanzang's disciple. There's a bit of awkwardness because of their fight, but once they go through the initial reintroduction, Erlang promises him his assistance, invites him to an impromptu feast, and then chats long into the night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1607-creticus","name":"Creticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T12:53:30-07:00","id":1097236,"title":"","content":"This preview killed all of my interest in this game at once.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>A Green Sun Destrier</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/77-kongurous","name":"kongurous","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar77_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"417"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T13:00:13-07:00","id":1097240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kongurous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1097178-confucius-is-a-god?p=1097236#post1097236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This preview killed all of my interest in this game at once.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, really?<br /> <br /> Care to dive a little deeper into that, because it pretty much had the opposite reaction from me.<br /> <br /> (i.e., it was interesting and introduced the Pantheon in a way that made me interested in more than just Sun Wukong, and made me excited all over again to get my hands on Scion,)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/728-crownedsun","name":"CrownedSun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar728_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"217"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T13:06:36-07:00","id":1097247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CrownedSun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1097178-confucius-is-a-god?p=1097240#post1097240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Huh, really?<br /> <br /> Care to dive a little deeper into that, because it pretty much had the opposite reaction from me.<br /> <br /> (i.e., it was interesting and introduced the Pantheon in a way that made me interested in more than just Sun Wukong, and made me excited all over again to get my hands on Scion,)</div> </div> </div> </div>The overly conversational tone is extremely bothersome, and I'm greatly incensed by the unironic Wu-Tang Clan references coupled with their presentation as a magical Chinese Illuminati, because I guess Yellow Peril is A-OK as long as you're couching it in kitschy pop culture references.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>A Green Sun Destrier</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/77-kongurous","name":"kongurous","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar77_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"417"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T13:17:08-07:00","id":1097257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kongurous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1097178-confucius-is-a-god?p=1097247#post1097247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The overly conversational tone is extremely bothersome, and I'm greatly incensed by the unironic Wu-Tang Clan references coupled with their presentation as a magical Chinese Illuminati, because I guess Yellow Peril is A-OK as long as you're couching it in kitschy pop culture references.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, no, you've got the references backwards.<br /> <br /> The Wu-Tang are a reference to <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wudang_quan\" target=\"_blank\">Wudang</a>. I can see the annoyance behind kitschy references, but it actually is a group of monks who do stick their noses into political affairs on occasion. If Taoist alchemy really does give you mystic powers, as it does in this game.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I'm not saying it's not mildly annoying to have the monks be a large shout-out, but really, it's hardly a deal-breaker, especially if they change it to be slightly less of a reference.<br /> <br /> *nudge nudge, hint hint*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 05-26-2017, 04:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T13:19:59-07:00","id":1097259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kongurous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1097178-confucius-is-a-god?p=1097247#post1097247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The overly conversational tone is extremely bothersome, and I'm greatly incensed by the unironic Wu-Tang Clan references coupled with their presentation as a magical Chinese Illuminati, because I guess Yellow Peril is A-OK as long as you're couching it in kitschy pop culture references.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It doesn't seem all that different from Tianxia or Wuxia and the web novels that come out of those genres today (of which I have read a few). Its interesting that you feel that it is associated with Yellow Peril, as I am personally quite sensitive to that and I didn't feel it too much. As for the conversational tone, since the Great Classics of Chinese Literature are mostly vernacular fiction, that seems quite appropriate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>How can I know if what I claim I know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I might not know? How can I know if what I claim I don't know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I do know?<br /> -Zhuangzi","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1715-ostarion","name":"Ostarion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1715_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T13:20:03-07:00","id":1097260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1097178-confucius-is-a-god?p=1097257#post1097257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yeah, no, you've got it exactly backwards.<br /> <br /> The Wu-Tang are a reference to <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wudang_quan\" target=\"_blank\">Wudang</a>. I can see the annoyance behind kitschy references, but it actually is a group of monks who do stick their noses into political affairs on occasion. If Taoist alchemy really does give you mystic powers, as it does in this game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm well aware of the existence of the Wudang Sect, that's where the rap group got their name. It is still the lowest of low hanging fruit and still edging onto what is a harmful stereotype.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>A Green Sun Destrier</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/77-kongurous","name":"kongurous","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar77_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"417"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T13:29:21-07:00","id":1097267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kongurous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1097178-confucius-is-a-god?p=1097260#post1097260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm well aware of the existence of the Wudang Sect, that's where the rap group got their name. It is still the lowest of low hanging fruit and still edging onto what is a harmful stereotype.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I do agree that it is a stereotype, especially in our own literature and popular novels. But I think the best way to solve the problem is to just add more sects and clans as that list of followers is quite small.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>How can I know if what I claim I know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I might not know? How can I know if what I claim I don't know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I do know?<br /> -Zhuangzi","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1715-ostarion","name":"Ostarion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1715_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T13:36:33-07:00","id":1097269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kongurous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1097178-confucius-is-a-god?p=1097260#post1097260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm well aware of the existence of the Wudang Sect, that's where the rap group got their name. It is still the lowest of low hanging fruit and still edging onto what is a harmful stereotype.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a tougher line to walk than you seem to acknowledging given that the trope of the ancient Taoist priesthood turned conspiracy is a cornerstone in Chinese wuxia cinema. The harm arises in Western media from the lack of Asian protagonists, and instead colonial white saviors battling the evil Asians. Something becomes a &quot;stereotype&quot; by being treated as representative, which I don't believe this is doing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T13:44:16-07:00","id":1097272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ostarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1097178-confucius-is-a-god?p=1097259#post1097259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It doesn't seem all that different from Tianxia or Wuxia and the web novels that come out of those genres today (of which I have read a few). Its interesting that you feel that it is associated with Yellow Peril, as I am personally quite sensitive to that and I didn't feel it too much. As for the conversational tone, since the Great Classics of Chinese Literature are mostly vernacular fiction, that seems quite appropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's xianxia.<br /> <br /> Wuxia is about mortal but often superhuman martial artists dealing with mortal affairs. Xianxia is much more fantastical in nature, which makes sense because it's focused on people attempting to become immortals. Unfortunately, a lot of xianxia stories are nothing but noxious power fantasies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1607-creticus","name":"Creticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T13:50:23-07:00","id":1097277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Creticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1097178-confucius-is-a-god?p=1097272#post1097272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's xianxia.<br /> <br /> Wuxia is about mortal but often superhuman martial artists dealing with mortal affairs. Xianxia is much more fantastical in nature, which makes sense because it's focused on people attempting to become immortals. Unfortunately, a lot of xianxia stories are nothing but noxious power fantasies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sturgeon's Law hardly seems like a problem with xianxia alone. So are a lot of Western superhero stories. The first thing that sprung to mind for a noxious power fantasy are a lot of A1 Pictures' work, a Japanese company.<br /> <br /> Depends on the author, I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T14:10:10-07:00","id":1097286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Creticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1097178-confucius-is-a-god?p=1097272#post1097272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's xianxia.<br /> <br /> Wuxia is about mortal but often superhuman martial artists dealing with mortal affairs. Xianxia is much more fantastical in nature, which makes sense because it's focused on people attempting to become immortals. Unfortunately, a lot of xianxia stories are nothing but noxious power fantasies.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, yes , and there are a lot of other categories related to it. Plenty of examples, written by both traditional and internet authors. Wuxia Chongsheng being a recent webnovel I am reading features them. Tianxia was something I mentioned regarding the RPG which features the stereotypical Triad as well.<br /> <br /> But yes there are numerous Yi yin genres of all types, and any one of them can have plenty of Chinese stereotypes","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>How can I know if what I claim I know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I might not know? How can I know if what I claim I don't know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I do know?<br /> -Zhuangzi","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1715-ostarion","name":"Ostarion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1715_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T14:41:54-07:00","id":1097301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1097178-confucius-is-a-god?p=1097277#post1097277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sturgeon's Law hardly seems like a problem with xianxia alone. So are a lot of Western superhero stories. The first thing that sprung to mind for a noxious power fantasy are a lot of A1 Pictures' work, a Japanese company.<br /> <br /> Depends on the author, I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>A1 Pictures is not an inappropriate comparison, considering the number of LN adaptations that they make.<br /> <br /> However, if the stereotypical Japanese LN is some dude being looked down upon in spite of his special powers building a harem of vapid cutouts, the stereotypical xianxia story is some dude being looked down upon in spite of his special powers building a harem of vapid cutouts while killing lots and lots of people. There are exceptions to the rule such as Ze Tian Ji, but xianxia protagonists are basically murderhobos, complete with grinding enlightenment like it's leveling up in a video game.<br /> <br /> I get that this is because it's aimed at an audience who are dissatisfied with the current state of things, but it doesn't change the fact that it's pretty unpleasant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1607-creticus","name":"Creticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T15:31:33-07:00","id":1097325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1097178-confucius-is-a-god?p=1097269#post1097269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a tougher line to walk than you seem to acknowledging given that the trope of the ancient Taoist priesthood turned conspiracy is a cornerstone in Chinese wuxia cinema. The harm arises in Western media from the lack of Asian protagonists, and instead colonial white saviors battling the evil Asians.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm reminded of the rather short lived 1956 Atlas (now Marvel) Comics series &quot;Yellow Claw&quot;, which was clearly inspired by Sax Rhomer's Fu Manchu series, with the interesting (to me, at least) subversion that the heroic protagonist was a Chinese-American FBI agent. <br /> <br /> Something else I always found interesting was that Fu Manchu and his various doppelg\u00e4ngers are almost always presented as being the superior of the heroes. They come across as Nietzsche's hyper-man, a sort of amoral version of the Confucian ideal of a jenzi gentleman. Or perhaps, as Warren Ellis presented it in Planetary, they really are a Doc Savage-style heroic superman, just concerned with their own nation/culture's needs and ideals, which happens to put them in conflict with Western governments. But I also rather enjoyed Jeff Parker's take that the over-the-top stereotypical villainy is just a ruse to distract the ignorant gweilo from what's really going on behind the scenes. I find that much more interesting than the utterly joyless straight forward self-righteousness of DC's Ra's al Ghul. <br /> <br /> At this point, I think I really would sometime like to take a stab at playing a Scion of the Celestial Bureaucracy who is a Confucian gentleman aspiring to become a full fledged sage, having created this vast network of agents and plots, all toward the goal of improving society through cultivating virtue and maintaining ethics. Naturally, this is unacceptable to most world governments, East and West, because, to quote Mel Brooks, &quot;We've got to protect our phony baloney jobs!&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T15:50:00-07:00","id":1097335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Creticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1097178-confucius-is-a-god?p=1097301#post1097301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, if the stereotypical Japanese LN is some dude being looked down upon in spite of his special powers building a harem of vapid cutouts, the stereotypical xianxia story is some dude being looked down upon in spite of his special powers building a harem of vapid cutouts while killing lots and lots of people.</div> </div> </div> </div>And looting. Can't forget about all the treasure caves and ruins that only open when the dude just happens to be a high enough level to raid them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T18:36:37-07:00","id":1097383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1097178-confucius-is-a-god?p=1097335#post1097335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And looting. Can't forget about all the treasure caves and ruins that only open when the dude just happens to be a high enough level to raid them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Xianxia draws a lot from video games. It's another thing that it shares with its Japanese isekai counterparts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1607-creticus","name":"Creticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T19:26:12-07:00","id":1097395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kongurous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1097178-confucius-is-a-god?p=1097260#post1097260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm well aware of the existence of the Wudang Sect, that's where the rap group got their name. It is still the lowest of low hanging fruit and still edging onto what is a harmful stereotype.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bracket off the Wu Tang clan reference from your assessment: What's the actual problem with the Wudang as presented? They're a historical meddling religious sect, and the idea of an illuminati style group reaches across cultures let alone China which has a million religious or philosophical sects in the background. It isn't like the Tao Te Ching isn't full of political advice on how to meddle or anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T09:34:19-07:00","id":1097556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1097178-confucius-is-a-god?p=1097395#post1097395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Bracket off the Wu Tang clan reference from your assessment: What's the actual problem with the Wudang as presented? They're a historical meddling religious sect, and the idea of an illuminati style group reaches across cultures let alone China which has a million religious or philosophical sects in the background. It isn't like the Tao Te Ching isn't full of political advice on how to medd